    "legacy": "The legacy of St. Vincent Ferrer extends far beyond a single feast on April 5. Performed miracles including raising the dead and healing the blind Patron of builders and orphanages in Valencia Popes, councils, and local churches have confirmed this saint's importance through canonization, liturgical ranking, and the inclusion of their name in missals worldwide. Artists, composers, and writers continue to depict St. Vincent Ferrer because holiness is attractive — it answers the deepest hunger of the human heart. For catechists and parents, this saint offers ready-made material: a story of virtue, a date to circle on the calendar, and a name to invoke at bedtime. For scholars, the same life opens windows into the history of Valencia, Spain and the development of Catholic spirituality. In every case, the legacy is the same: St. Vincent Ferrer still leads souls to Christ.",
