    "intro": "St. Zita of Lucca is the Catholic Saint of the Day for April 27 — a confessor and servant of the Church whose intercession Catholics seek especially as patron of domestic workers, housekeepers, and Lucca. Domestic servant known for charity and miracles over forty-eight years On this feast, parishes, schools, and families around the world remember St. Zita of Lucca through Mass, prayer, and acts of charity aligned with this saint's legacy. Whether you discovered this page searching for today's saint, preparing a homily, or deepening your devotional life, this guide offers a complete biography: origins in Monsagrati, Italy, key moments from 1212–1272, and the reasons this holy figure remains among the most beloved saints in Catholic tradition. Shared food with the poor and cared for sick prisoners",
