    "intro": "St. Anthony Mary Zaccaria is the Catholic Saint of the Day for July 5 — a confessor and servant of the Church whose intercession Catholics seek especially as patron of physicians, Barnabite order, and laity. Founder of the Barnabites to reform clergy and laity in Milan On this feast, parishes, schools, and families around the world remember St. Anthony Mary Zaccaria through Mass, prayer, and acts of charity aligned with this saint's legacy. Whether you discovered this page searching for today's saint, preparing a homily, or deepening your devotional life, this guide offers a complete biography: origins in Cremona, Italy, key moments from 1502–1539, and the reasons this holy figure remains among the most beloved saints in Catholic tradition. Pioneer of forty-hour Eucharistic adoration devotions",
